more women fighting breast cancer across  southern nevada will get the help and  support they need after our community  helped raise 77 thousand dollars in one  day as kirsten joyce shows us that's all  thanks to the caring place program and  the ladies pink tea charitable golf  tournament  nikki you're a cancer survivor of 15  years how does it make you feel to see  all these people come out and support  other survivors it's amazing it truly is  nikki rudy is part of a sisterhood that  no one asked to be a part of when  someone's diagnosed it's a tragic and a  horrible situation and many don't know  where to turn so they turn to the caring  place and when they do they get help  with food basic needs mortgage and rent  payments medication hands-on services  like massage therapy and reiki the  caring place is a program of nevada  childhood cancer foundation with  professionals assisting women and their  families every step of the way many of  the clients are now coming to us and  needing individual counseling support  and our support group so those have  grown  greatly over this time this past year  has given us so many challenges and  breast cancer is no exception for 19  years funds raised at the ping t  charitable golf tournament at southern  highlands golf club have helped women in  the fight of their lives ladies what's  the cheer  our partnership with the caring place is  something that's extremely special not  just for us but for our entire club and  our community and the hope of one day  finding a cure kirsten joyce live local  now
 

